! An aluminium (100) slab -- five layers and 16 bohr of vacuum -- as the
! *convergence* benchmark, not a timing one.
!
! Everything else in this directory is a single-k-point cost-per-iteration case
! for tools/compare_qe.py. This one is here for the opposite reason: it is a
! system where the number of iterations is the interesting quantity, because the
! screening is inhomogeneous. Half the cell is a metal, where the dielectric
! function diverges as q^-2 at long wavelength, and half is vacuum, where there
! is no screening at all. Plain Anderson mixing amplifies the long-wavelength
! charge transfer between the two and reaches +105 Ry on its second iteration
! before recovering; Kerker preconditioning helps, and cannot fix it, because a
! single Thomas-Fermi screening length is wrong in one half of the cell whatever
! it is set to.
!
! It is the case PLAN.md P22's solver comparison is measured on, and the case
! tests/regression/test_scf_solvers.py checks the residual and its Jacobian on.
! Five layers and 2x2 k-points are the smallest choice that keeps the physics
! and runs in a few seconds.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, nat = 5, ntyp = 1, ecutwfc = 12.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-8, mixing_beta = 0.7, electron_maxstep = 300
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pz-vbc.UPF
CELL_PARAMETERS bohr
 5.303301 0.000000  0.000000
 0.000000 5.303301  0.000000
 0.000000 0.000000 31.000000
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Al 0.0000 0.0000 0.258065
 Al 0.5000 0.5000 0.379032
 Al 0.0000 0.0000 0.500000
 Al 0.5000 0.5000 0.620968
 Al 0.0000 0.0000 0.741935
K_POINTS automatic
 2 2 1 0 0 0
